  "worked_solution": "The moment of inertia of a plane lamina in the shape of a region $D$ about an axis of rotation $l$ is given by\n\n$$\n{I}_{l}={\u222c}_{D}\\lambda (x,y)[r(x,y)]^{2}\\,\\text{d}A,\n$$\n\nwhere $\\lambda (x,y)$ is the mass density function of the lamina, and $r(x,y)$ is the distance from the line $l$ to the point $(x,y)$ on $D.$\n\nThe distance between a point on $D$ and the line $x=1$ is given by\n\n$$\nr(x,y)=|x-1|.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the moment of inertia about the line $x=1$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{I}_{l} & ={\u222c}_{D}\\lambda (x,y)[r(x,y)]^{2}\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{1}^{2}3(x+y)|x-1{|}^{2}\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{1}^{2}3(x+y)(x-1)^{2}\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}{[\\frac{3(x+y)^{2}}{2}(x-1)^{2}]}_{1}^{2}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}\\frac{3((x+2)^{2}-(x+1)^{2})}{2}(x-1)^{2}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{2}{\\int }_{0}^{1}(2x+3)(x-1)^{2}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{2}{\\int }_{0}^{1}(2{x}^{3}-{x}^{2}-4x+3)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{2}{[\\frac{{x}^{4}}{2}-\\frac{{x}^{3}}{3}-2{x}^{2}+3x]}_{0}^{1} \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{2}((\\frac{1}{2}-\\frac{1}{3}-2+3)-0) \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{2}(\\frac{7}{6}) \\\\  & =\\frac{7}{4}.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
